# nr-relay-twin-data

## Cargo and workspace edits

None. The suite is JSON scenarios under native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/tests/twin/scenarios/data/ (run by the existing
`twin_scenarios` and `twin_crossover` tests of tests/twin/main.rs) and the ledger file tests/ledger/nr-relay-twin-data.json.
compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING: no name is added or removed.

## One edit the suite needs in a file of another task (native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/tests/twin/normalise.rs)

Every scenario that opens a phone leg ends with the relay's own log line for it:

    [relay] phone leg closed client=<first 8 hex of a random UUID> code=<n> reason=<text> lived=<n>ms

(lib/relay-legs.mjs runClientLeg on the Node side, logline::phone_leg_closed on the Rust side). The client prefix is
random and `lived` is a duration, so no two runs agree on this line and `twin_harness_self_check`, `twin_scenarios`
and `twin_crossover` fail on the first scenario with a phone (data/devices_across_runtimes, data/device_revocation_across_runtimes,
data/device_store_placed_rows, data/switch_rehearsal_live_traffic, and every phone scenario of the identity and legs suites).
In `Normaliser::value`, for an event whose `"ev"` is `"log"`, apply to its `"line"` string, after the existing masks:

  1. `client=([0-9a-f]{8})\b` -> `client=<id:N>`, N taken from the same first-appearance table `identifiers` uses
     (key: the 8 characters), so two legs stay distinguishable;
  2. `lived=\d+ms` -> `lived=<ms>`.

Nothing else of a log line is masked (code and reason stay compared). Until this is applied, only the scenarios without
a phone leg (data/feedback_across_runtimes, data/feedback_records_placed, data/web_push_across_runtimes) can pass.

## Timing the scenarios rely on

data/feedback_across_runtimes sets feedbackOptions.baseDelayMs to 5000 and waits 7000 ms after the switch for the retry
of the pending record; the first segment of that scenario is shorter than 5 s by construction (two requests and a 500 ms
wait). The host contract of tests/twin/node/relay-host.mjs already carries feedbackOptions, handshakeStallMs and
livenessProbeMs (the rehearsal and the device scenarios set the last two to 600000 so no handshake-stall log line appears).
